1. (Currently amended) A system, comprising:
a processor node comprising a processor and a network interface;
a plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node comprises a memory and a network interface;
a communication network configured to interconnect said processor node and said plurality of memory nodes via said network interfaces according to a network topology, wherein each of said memory nodes is removed from said processor node by a respective number of network hops according to said network topology;
wherein said processor node is configured to:
broadcast a memory request message comprising a unique identifier of a given memory request and a requested memory size to a subset of said plurality of memory nodes;
send a confirmation message comprising the unique identifier to a particular one of the subset of memory nodes in response to receiving a reservation acknowledgment message from said particular one of the memory nodes, wherein the confirmation message includes __a commitment to allocate the requested memory size__;
and access memory on the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a commit message from the particular one of the memory nodes indicating that the memory has been allocated and reserved for the given memory request __according to the commitment indicated in the confirmation message__.

2. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the processor node is further configured to create a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value, __and a state indicator tracking the reservation status__, and wherein if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to a given message being sent by the processor node, the processor node is further configured to re-send the given message __or cancel the reservation__.

3. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is configured to reserve a portion of memory at least as large as the requested memory size __in response to determining that the requested memory size is available__ and to send a reservation acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving the given memory request if the given memory request may be satisfied by the particular one of the memory nodes.

4. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to create a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value, __and a state indicator tracking the reservation status__, and wherein if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to a given message being sent by the particular one of the memory nodes, the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to re-send the given message __or release the reserved memory__.

5. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a commit message comprising the unique identifier __and confirmation that the memory allocation is complete__ to the processor node in response to receiving the confirmation message from the processor node.

6. (Originally presented) The system of claim 1, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a read acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving a read request message comprising the unique identifier from the processor node subsequent to receiving the confirmation message, and wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to send a write acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving a write request message comprising the unique identifier from the processor node subsequent to receiving the confirmation message.

7. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein the processor node is further configured to send a reject message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes to indicate that it no longer requires access to the memory allocated for the given memory request, __wherein the reject message is sent only after the confirmation message has been received by the particular one of the memory nodes__.

8. (Originally presented) The system of claim 7, wherein the particular one of the memory nodes is further configured to free the memory allocated for the given memory request and to send a reject acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving the reject message from the processor node.

9. (Originally presented) The system of claim 8, wherein the processor node is further configured to send a reject confirmation message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving the reject acknowledgement message from the particular one of the memory nodes.

10. (Currently amended) The system of claim 1, wherein each memory node of said subset is removed from said processor node by no more than a given number of network hops; and wherein if no memory node of said subset indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request __within a specified time period__, the processor node is further configured to increase said given number of network hops and to broadcast the memory request message to a second subset of said plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node of said second subset is removed from said processor node by no more than said increased given number of network hops.

11. (Currently amended) The system of claim 10, wherein if no memory node of said second subset indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request __within the specified time period__, the processor node is further configured to continue to increase said given number of network hops and to broadcast the memory request message to a corresponding subset of said plurality of memory nodes, wherein each memory node of said corresponding subset is removed from said processor node by no more than said increased given number of network hops, until at least one of the following occurs: one or more of said plurality of memory nodes indicates that it can satisfy the given memory request in response to receiving the given memory request, said processor node has broadcast the memory request message to each of said plurality of memory nodes, or a time-out condition has been met.

12. (Currently amended) A method, comprising:
a processor node broadcasting a memory request message comprising a unique identifier of a given memory request and a requested memory size to a plurality of memory nodes, wherein said plurality of memory nodes and said processor node are interconnected via a communication network according to a network topology;
the processor node sending a confirmation message __comprising the unique identifier and a commitment to allocate the requested memory size__ to a particular one of the plurality of memory nodes in response to receiving a reservation acknowledgment message from said particular one of the plurality of memory nodes;
and the processor accessing memory on the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a commit message from the particular one of the memory nodes indicating that the memory has been allocated and reserved for the given memory request __according to the commitment indicated in the confirmation message__.

13. (Currently amended) The method of claim 12, further comprising:
the processor node creating a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value, __and a state indicator tracking the reservation status__;
and the processor node re-sending a given message if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to the given message being sent by the processor node __or canceling the reservation__.

14. (Currently amended) The method of claim 12, further comprising the particular one of the memory nodes reserving a portion of memory at least as large as the requested memory size __in response to determining that the requested memory size is available__ and sending a reservation acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving the given memory request if the given memory request may be satisfied by the particular one of the memory nodes.

15. (Currently amended) The method of claim 12, further comprising:
the particular one of the memory nodes creating a reservation structure for the given memory request comprising the unique identifier, a timeout value __dependent on a time-to-live value included in the memory request message__, __and a state indicator tracking the reservation status__;
and the particular one of the memory nodes re-sending a given message if a timer reaches the timeout value before a reply message is received in response to the given message being sent by the particular one of the memory nodes __or releasing the reserved memory__.

16. (Currently amended) The method of claim 12, further comprising:
the processor node sending a reject message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes to indicate that it no longer requires access to the memory allocated for the given memory request, __wherein the reject message is sent only after the confirmation message has been received by the particular one of the memory nodes__;
the particular one of the memory nodes freeing the memory allocated for the given memory request and sending a reject acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving the reject message from the processor node;
and the processor node sending a reject confirmation message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving the reject acknowledgement message from the particular one of the memory nodes.

17. (Currently amended) A processor node, comprising:
an input/output interface configured for communicating with a communication network, wherein said communication network is configured to interconnect a plurality of memory nodes according to a network topology;
and execution logic configured to:
broadcast a memory request message comprising a unique identifier of a given memory request and a requested memory size to the plurality of memory nodes;
send a confirmation message __comprising the unique identifier and a commitment to allocate the requested memory size__ to a particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a reservation acknowledgment message from said particular one of the memory nodes;
and access memory on the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a commit message from the particular one of the memory nodes indicating that the memory has been allocated and reserved for the given memory request __according to the commitment indicated in the confirmation message__.

18. (Currently amended) The processor node of claim 17, wherein the execution logic is further configured to:
send a reject message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes to indicate that it no longer requires access to the memory allocated for the given memory request, __wherein the reject message is sent only after the confirmation message has been received by the particular one of the memory nodes__;
and send a reject confirmation message comprising the unique identifier to the particular one of the memory nodes in response to receiving a reject acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier from the particular one of the memory nodes.

19. (Currently amended) A memory node, comprising:
a memory;
an input/output interface configured for communicating with a communication network, wherein said communication network is configured to interconnect a processor node and a plurality of memory nodes according to a network topology;
and execution logic configured to:
receive a memory request message comprising a unique identifier of a given memory request and a requested memory size from the processor node;
reserve a portion of memory at least as large as the requested memory size __in response to determining that the requested memory size is available__ and send a reservation acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving the given memory request if the given memory request may be satisfied by the memory node;
and send a commit message comprising the unique identifier __and confirmation that the memory allocation is complete__ to the processor node in response to receiving a confirmation message __comprising a commitment to allocate the requested memory size__ from the processor node.

20. (Currently amended) The memory node of claim 19, wherein the execution logic is further configured to:
free the memory allocated for the given memory request and send a reject acknowledgement message comprising the unique identifier to the processor node in response to receiving a reject message __sent only after the confirmation message has been received by the memory node__ from the processor node.
